verdict.handoff_to_code:
Verified: from claude.ai/design, Export offers \"Handoff to Claude Code\", either \"Send to local coding agent\" or \"Send to Claude Code Web\". The bundle holds the project's design files, the chat, and a README telling the model how to read the designs, plus a prompt carrying the bundle URL (Academy tutorial). A secondary source (dev.to) says the bundle is HTML/CSS/JS with screenshots of each state and a README naming the target stack.

From Claude Code, /design can import a design into the codebase, export the code as a live prototype, or build the whole thing (help centre). The /design canvas publishes artboards, and you tell Claude which one to implement (week-34 note). Other exports are .zip, PDF, PPTX, standalone HTML, Google Slides (claude.ai/design only) and partner tools.

Anthropic's \"continues from your existing work instead of starting over from a screenshot\" assumes the component library was synced. For Wombat it cannot be, because /design-sync is React-only, so the handoff is effectively a visual spec.

Claude Code must translate the HTML/React output into Razor components and app.css tokens under DESIGN.md's rules:

- no hex outside :root;
- Lucide icons through Icon.razor;
- no inline <style> in page .razor files;
- no Bootstrap, Tailwind or jQuery;
- self-hosted fonts, to satisfy CSP font-src 'self';
- the static-SSR versus InteractiveServer split;
- the framework-generated validation and reconnect markup.

wmedia.es describes this path for non-React stacks: design in Claude Design, pull the artboard, have Claude Code implement it against the repo. Verify each implemented flow with the bUnit tests and a browser check per role, as the repo's existing definition of done requires.
